Primitive Data Types: 

1. Integral Numbers: [-, +] i.e saare whole numbers not 0.

byte, short, int, long.

ex: Chai cup se pite hai na ki balti se and nahate balti se na ki cup se.
    So, we will use as per our requirement i.e capacity.
    byte age = 20;
    short age1 = 20;
    int age2 = 20;
    long age3 = 20;

2. Decimal Numbers:
float, double.

If you want more precision then use double otherwise float is also fine.

3. Characters:
For every character there is a corresponding number in the Unicode character set.
char a = 'A'; // 65 in Unicode

